It is Saturday morning, and I am finished at the café.
I have just wiped down the last table.
I untie my apron and put it on a chair.
Today I have had a short shift.
Last week I worked until three o'clock.
That day we were very busy all day.
But today we have only had a few guests.
The sun is shining outside, and it is a beautiful summer day.
Tonight there is a big bonfire down by the sea.
I am looking forward to seeing it very much.
I take my phone and write a message to Eva.
I ask her, "Are we still meeting tonight?"
I also write that I am already off work.
"I finished early today, so I am ready," I write.
Eva replies almost immediately.
"Yes, of course!" she replies.
"I have just bought fresh strawberries."
"See you at the beach later," she writes.
I smile and take my bag.
Then I walk out into the warm summer weather.
